\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Instability of the isolated throat. (a)~Minimal areal radius from exact static data at refinement levels 2--4. The exact solution ($R_\star $, dotted) is held until truncation noise excites the unstable mode: level 3 (dashed) collapses, level 4 (solid) inflates, level 2 (grey) dies of an origin failure first (cross). Dots mark where the scan loses the throat; muted lines carry the last reading. (b)~$|R-R_0|/R_0$: one exponential mode with a level-dependent sign; gold, small-amplitude fits, $\tau =5.12/5.23$ at levels 3/4, the linear rate; larger departures slow. (c)~Level 3 with declared seeds, Eq.~\eqref  {eq:seed}: $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ (heavy), $\pm 10^{-3}$ (light) and, heaviest, $\pm 0.1$, which both collapse; dashed, outward kicks. Twins cross at $t_\times \simeq 13.0$ independent of $\varepsilon $. Gold: local exponential fits; crosses, at the last reading: deaths at the compactified origin, $t=40.1$ ($+10^{-3}$), $14.1$ ($+0.1$) and $15.2$ ($-0.1$). Their constraint norms are Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(a,b). Unless a seed is declared, the grid's truncation noise picks the branch. (d)~The throat in motion (Sec.~\ref {sec:single:moving}): the exact Lorentz-boosted throat (dash-dot, $p=0.45$, level 3) against the resting level-3 arm (grey). It rides $R_\star $ to $t\approx 25$ and then collapses on the level-3 mode, dying at $t=44.67$: the fate and its rate are the resting throat's, carried with the motion.}}{8}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:single_throat}{{3}{8}{Instability of the isolated throat. (a)~Minimal areal radius from exact static data at refinement levels 2--4. The exact solution ($R_\star $, dotted) is held until truncation noise excites the unstable mode: level 3 (dashed) collapses, level 4 (solid) inflates, level 2 (grey) dies of an origin failure first (cross). Dots mark where the scan loses the throat; muted lines carry the last reading. (b)~$|R-R_0|/R_0$: one exponential mode with a level-dependent sign; gold, small-amplitude fits, $\tau =\clmTauLevelThree /\clmTauLevelFour $ at levels 3/4, the linear rate; larger departures slow. (c)~Level 3 with declared seeds, Eq.~\eqref {eq:seed}: $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ (heavy), $\pm 10^{-3}$ (light) and, heaviest, $\pm 0.1$, which both collapse; dashed, outward kicks. Twins cross at $t_\times \simeq \clmCrossingMean $ independent of $\varepsilon $. Gold: local exponential fits; crosses, at the last reading: deaths at the compactified origin, $t=\clmKickThreeDeath $ ($+10^{-3}$), $\clmCeilingDeathPlus $ ($+0.1$) and $\clmCeilingDeathMinus $ ($-0.1$). Their constraint norms are Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(a,b). Unless a seed is declared, the grid's truncation noise picks the branch. (d)~The throat in motion (Sec.~\ref {sec:single:moving}): the exact Lorentz-boosted throat (dash-dot, $p=\clmSpiralMomentumFlyby $, level 3) against the resting level-3 arm (grey). It rides $R_\star $ to $t\approx \clmBoostMovingPeakTime $ and then collapses on the level-3 mode, dying at $t=\clmBoostMovingDeath $: the fate and its rate are the resting throat's, carried with the motion}{figure.3}{}}
