\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {V}{\ignorespaces The drainhole clock in physical units: the production throat ($R_\star =3.89\,M$) scaled by its ADM mass $M$. $\tau =5.12\,M$ is the e-fold time (Sec.~\ref {sec:single:instability}); the last three columns are the measured times to a horizon for the two declared kicks, both outward ($\varepsilon >0$, the collapsing sign; Fig.~\ref {fig:single_throat}(c)), and an upper bound for truncation noise (Sec.~\ref {sec:single:branching}). Intermediate seeds follow $t_{\rm  BH}\simeq 11\,M+\tau \ln (10^{-2}/\varepsilon )$ at matched horizon radius: $22.8\,M$ at $10^{-3}$, whose first MOTS, born smaller, comes at $25\,M$.}}{10}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:scales}{{V}{10}{The drainhole clock in physical units: the production throat ($R_\star =\clmRstarShort \,M$) scaled by its ADM mass $M$. $\tau =\clmTauLevelThree \,M$ is the e-fold time (Sec.~\ref {sec:single:instability}); the last three columns are the measured times to a horizon for the two declared kicks, both outward ($\varepsilon >0$, the collapsing sign; Fig.~\ref {fig:single_throat}(c)), and an upper bound for truncation noise (Sec.~\ref {sec:single:branching}). Intermediate seeds follow $t_{\rm BH}\simeq \clmHorizonTimeEpsTwo \,M+\tau \ln (10^{-2}/\varepsilon )$ at matched horizon radius: $\clmLawEpsThree \,M$ at $10^{-3}$, whose first MOTS, born smaller, comes at $\clmHorizonTimeEpsThree \,M$}{table.5}{}}
