\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The head-on merger ($d=8$ from rest, $p=0$, opposite signs) on matched, solved data ($M_{\rm  ADM}=2.3573$), and the black hole it makes. One evolution in three segments (faint dashed rules at the seams, $t=35$ and $50.8$; levels named in each panel; Sec.~\ref {sec:headon:wall}): level 5 to a NaN in $h_{11}$ at the merged core at $t=38.845$, inside the MOTS (its overrun grey to the death cross in (c)--(e)); level 6 from segment 1's $t=35$ checkpoint through the failure window; level 4 to $t=100$ with no NaN. In-code $\Psi _4$ is identical on both overlaps. (a)~Areal radius and (b)~Misner--Sharp mass of the common MOTS. Gold: the spectral finder's history (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots}, one row per plotfile, the three replay segments joined), born at $t=18$ with $R=5.634$ ($M_{\rm  MS}=2.817$) and shrinking---regrowing by at most $0.34\%$---toward the Schwarzschild sphere of the pair's mass: $R=4.7787$ and $M_{\rm  MS}=2.3894$ at $t=100$, $1.4\%$ above $2M_{\rm  ADM}$ and $1.4\%$ above $M_{\rm  ADM}$. Grey dashes: the round star scan, the inner bound of Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots}, late and small at birth and blind over $t=26$--$35$ (Sec.~\ref {sec:headon:contact}). Rules: one isolated throat, $R_\star =3.8895$; $\sqrt  2R_\star $, a sphere with both throats' area; $2M_{\rm  ADM}$ ($M_{\rm  ADM}$ in (b)). (c)~Separation of the $\chi $ pits. (d)~$\max |K|$. (e)~Grid maxima of $|\phi |$ (solid) and $|\Pi |$ (dashed): the field is swallowed. Gold dotted rule: horizon birth. Movie: Video~3; \href  {https://youtu.be/3sx9GHRTYVs}{\nolinkurl  {youtu.be/3sx9GHRTYVs}}.}}{12}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:headon_collapse}{{6}{12}{The head-on merger ($d=\clmHeadonSeparation $ from rest, $p=0$, opposite signs) on matched, solved data ($M_{\rm ADM}=\clmHeadonCsmAdmMass $), and the black hole it makes. One evolution in three segments (faint dashed rules at the seams, $t=\clmHeadonCsmSeamOne $ and $\clmHeadonCsmSeamTwo $; levels named in each panel; Sec.~\ref {sec:headon:wall}): level 5 to a NaN in $h_{11}$ at the merged core at $t=\clmHeadonCsmNanTime $, inside the MOTS (its overrun grey to the death cross in (c)--(e)); level 6 from segment 1's $t=35$ checkpoint through the failure window; level 4 to $t=100$ with no NaN. In-code $\Psi _4$ is identical on both overlaps. (a)~Areal radius and (b)~Misner--Sharp mass of the common MOTS. Gold: the spectral finder's history (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots}, one row per plotfile, the three replay segments joined), born at $t=\clmHeadonCsmMotsTime $ with $R=\clmHeadonCsmMotsRadius $ ($M_{\rm MS}=\clmHeadonCsmMotsMass $) and shrinking---regrowing by at most $\clmHeadonCsmRegrow \%$---toward the Schwarzschild sphere of the pair's mass: $R=\clmHeadonCsmEndRadius $ and $M_{\rm MS}=\clmHeadonCsmEndMass $ at $t=100$, $\clmHeadonCsmEndOverSchw \%$ above $2M_{\rm ADM}$ and $\clmHeadonCsmEndMassOverAdm \%$ above $M_{\rm ADM}$. Grey dashes: the round star scan, the inner bound of Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots}, late and small at birth and blind over $t=26$--$35$ (Sec.~\ref {sec:headon:contact}). Rules: one isolated throat, $R_\star =\clmRstar $; $\sqrt 2R_\star $, a sphere with both throats' area; $2M_{\rm ADM}$ ($M_{\rm ADM}$ in (b)). (c)~Separation of the $\chi $ pits. (d)~$\max |K|$. (e)~Grid maxima of $|\phi |$ (solid) and $|\Pi |$ (dashed): the field is swallowed. Gold dotted rule: horizon birth. Movie: Video~3; \href {https://youtu.be/3sx9GHRTYVs}{\nolinkurl {youtu.be/3sx9GHRTYVs}}}{figure.6}{}}
