\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Every source at one calibration: total mass $30\,M_\odot $ at $10$ Mpc, each record in units of its own total mass; the vacuum twin is two black holes with the separation and momentum of the $d=12$, $p=0.12$ arm (Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:capture}). (a)~Upper envelopes of $|r\Psi _4|M$ at the innermost sphere, aligned at each peak: fly-by loudest ($1.4\times 10^{-1}$) to lone throat ($3.1\times 10^{-3}$). (b)~Strain amplitude spectral densities over the aLIGO design floor (gold), each from its own low-frequency corner (one cycle per record, ticked). The curves are falling power laws (slopes $-4.0$ to $-5.8$) with no resolved maximum, so any ``peak'' read here is the corner $1/T$. Faint line: the Newtonian inspiral of the same binary, $|\tilde  h|\propto f^{-7/6}$ to its ISCO at $147$ Hz. (c)~Instantaneous frequency against the point-mass chirp (gold), the ISCO ($147$ Hz) and the equal-mass Kerr ringdown ($599$ Hz): the vacuum twin climbs the chirp and peaks at $fM=0.065$; no wormhole channel does (Sec.~\ref {sec:ligo:ringdown}). (d)~Energy radiated in the dominant multipole at the outermost sphere covering each record's window, the tick its change from the next sphere in; grey under each source, its vacuum control at the same $d$ and $p$. Open gold bars: published equal-mass vacuum values: head-on infall from rest at infinity, $5.5\times 10^{-4}$~\cite  {witek2010}; quasi-circular inspiral from infinite separation and merger, $4.84\times 10^{-2}$~\cite  {scheel2009}; all multipoles. Energies are band integrals of $|\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ r\Psi _4\,\mathrm  {d}t'|^2$ over one retarded window per record, ending at its trust or noise gate (the lone throat's at $t=58$, before its floor), at the spheres whose record covers it (the fly-by's inner two), doubled for $\pm m$; gravitational channel only. Movie of the vacuum twin: Video~10; \href  {https://youtu.be/NkcpGiJIxXI}{\nolinkurl  {youtu.be/NkcpGiJIxXI}}.}}{16}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gw_ligo}{{9}{16}{Every source at one calibration: total mass $\clmGwLigoMass \,M_\odot $ at $\clmGwLigoDist $ Mpc, each record in units of its own total mass; the vacuum twin is two black holes with the separation and momentum of the $d=12$, $p=\clmSpiralMomentumProd $ arm (Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:capture}). (a)~Upper envelopes of $|r\Psi _4|M$ at the innermost sphere, aligned at each peak: fly-by loudest ($\clmGwEnvPeakFlyby $) to lone throat ($\clmGwEnvPeakThroat $). (b)~Strain amplitude spectral densities over the aLIGO design floor (gold), each from its own low-frequency corner (one cycle per record, ticked). The curves are falling power laws (slopes $\clmGwSlopeShallow $ to $\clmGwSlopeSteep $) with no resolved maximum, so any ``peak'' read here is the corner $1/T$. Faint line: the Newtonian inspiral of the same binary, $|\tilde h|\propto f^{-7/6}$ to its ISCO at $\clmGwIscoHz $ Hz. (c)~Instantaneous frequency against the point-mass chirp (gold), the ISCO ($\clmGwIscoHz $ Hz) and the equal-mass Kerr ringdown ($\clmGwKerrHz $ Hz): the vacuum twin climbs the chirp and peaks at $fM=\clmGwTwinPeakFM $; no wormhole channel does (Sec.~\ref {sec:ligo:ringdown}). (d)~Energy radiated in the dominant multipole at the outermost sphere covering each record's window, the tick its change from the next sphere in; grey under each source, its vacuum control at the same $d$ and $p$. Open gold bars: published equal-mass vacuum values: head-on infall from rest at infinity, $\clmGwLitHeadonInfall $~\cite {witek2010}; quasi-circular inspiral from infinite separation and merger, $\clmGwLitCircular $~\cite {scheel2009}; all multipoles. Energies are band integrals of $|\int r\Psi _4\,\mathrm {d}t'|^2$ over one retarded window per record, ending at its trust or noise gate (the lone throat's at $t=\clmGwThroatEnergyCut $, before its floor), at the spheres whose record covers it (the fly-by's inner two), doubled for $\pm m$; gravitational channel only. Movie of the vacuum twin: Video~10; \href {https://youtu.be/NkcpGiJIxXI}{\nolinkurl {youtu.be/NkcpGiJIxXI}}}{figure.9}{}}
