\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Convergence. (a)~The static throat from exact data at levels 2--4: the three-level factor $Q=(R_2-R_3)/(R_3-R_4)$ of its minimal areal radius against the orders $n=2$, 3, 4 (rules); the dip at $t=16$ is one level-2 dump. (b)~Bowen--York, not production, data: $|r\Psi _4^{22}|$ at $R=20$ of the $d=12$, $p=0.12$ pair at throat level 5, its difference from level 4, and the difference made by refining the wave zone to half the base cell. (c)~Radiated energy on each sphere over the outermost sphere's, against $R/M$: the head-on, the $d=6$ merger and the fly-by (ink) and two vacuum controls (grey). (d)~The far-zone head-on of Fig.~\ref {fig:gw_gallery}(b) at finest $\Delta x=1/16$, $1/32$ and $1/64$: $|r\Psi _4^{20}|$ at $R=10$ and each neighbouring pair's difference, peaking at $0.55\%$ and $0.54\%$ of the peak. All three form the common MOTS at $t=18$, its $R$ and $M_{\rm  MS}$ equal between neighbouring levels to at most $0.08\%$, and the energy at $R=10$ converges at order $1.7$: differences $0.3\%$, then $0.09\%$. (e)~The same three runs' $t=100$ checkpoints: shell averages of $\mathcal  {H}_{\rm  ADM}$ against $r$ outside the common MOTS (gold rule, its largest coordinate extent), read on the shared level-4 grid; each halving of the interior cell moves them by $1.4\%$, then $0.4\%$. The outcome: orders $3.0$--$3.3$ (static throat; $2.2$--$2.3$ while the error of reading the exact data dominates), $1.7$ (head-on energy) and $1.7$ ($\mathcal  {H}_{\rm  ADM}$); the Bowen--York binary's waveform is resolved to $0.4\%$ of its peak, the energy converges in extraction radius and in resolution, and the interior's constraint violation does not leak past the horizon.}}{20}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:convergence}{{10}{20}{Convergence. (a)~The static throat from exact data at levels 2--4: the three-level factor $Q=(R_2-R_3)/(R_3-R_4)$ of its minimal areal radius against the orders $n=2$, 3, 4 (rules); the dip at $t=16$ is one level-2 dump. (b)~Bowen--York, not production, data: $|r\Psi _4^{22}|$ at $R=\clmExtractRadiusTwenty $ of the $d=12$, $p=\clmSpiralMomentumProd $ pair at throat level 5, its difference from level 4, and the difference made by refining the wave zone to half the base cell. (c)~Radiated energy on each sphere over the outermost sphere's, against $R/M$: the head-on, the $d=6$ merger and the fly-by (ink) and two vacuum controls (grey). (d)~The far-zone head-on of Fig.~\ref {fig:gw_gallery}(b) at finest $\Delta x=1/\clmConvFzDxLo $, $1/\clmConvFzDxMid $ and $1/\clmConvFzDxHi $: $|r\Psi _4^{20}|$ at $R=\clmExtractRadiusTen $ and each neighbouring pair's difference, peaking at $\clmConvFzPsiDiff \%$ and $\clmConvFzPsiDiffFine \%$ of the peak. All three form the common MOTS at $t=\clmConvFzMotsTime $, its $R$ and $M_{\rm MS}$ equal between neighbouring levels to at most $\clmConvFzMotsDiff \%$, and the energy at $R=\clmExtractRadiusTen $ converges at order $\clmConvFzOrder $: differences $\clmConvFzEnergyDiff \%$, then $\clmConvFzEnergyDiffFine \%$. (e)~The same three runs' $t=100$ checkpoints: shell averages of $\mathcal {H}_{\rm ADM}$ against $r$ outside the common MOTS (gold rule, its largest coordinate extent), read on the shared level-4 grid; each halving of the interior cell moves them by $\clmConvFzHamDiff \%$, then $\clmConvFzHamDiffFine \%$. The outcome: orders $\clmConvOrderEvolLo $--$\clmConvOrderEvolHi $ (static throat; $\clmConvOrderDataLo $--$\clmConvOrderDataHi $ while the error of reading the exact data dominates), $\clmConvFzOrder $ (head-on energy) and $\clmConvFzHamOrder $ ($\mathcal {H}_{\rm ADM}$); the Bowen--York binary's waveform is resolved to $\clmConvPsiLevelDiff \%$ of its peak, the energy converges in extraction radius and in resolution, and the interior's constraint violation does not leak past the horizon}{figure.10}{}}
